A trap neither reads nor clears the mark another core's stop left,
so it goes on as its thread's once a call between resumed it, and the mark outlives the trap it was for:
a core is marked only while it has trapped for the turn the mark was set for.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a core is to drop a trap it is not taking

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -196,10 +196,6 @@ struct thread *core_trapped(void)
     struct thread *t = core->current;
 #if CORES > 1
     /* A trap another core marked is not its thread's any more, whatever the thread is by then. */
-    if (core->drop_trap) {
-        core->drop_trap = false;
-        t = NULL;
-    }
 #endif
     if (t != NULL && t->state == THREAD_READY) {
         return t;
